# Standing decisions

The owner's decisions and the defaults taken under them, in one place, so an agent follows them instead of
re-deriving or contradicting them. Read before you plan. A decision is changed only by the owner, or by a later row
that says it supersedes this one. An agent that disagrees says so with evidence on a ticket, and does not act against
a standing row. When the portal's decisions registry is available for this project, it imports this file and becomes
the registry.

Conventions: ids are `D-1`, `D-2`, ... in order, stable, never renumbered or reused. One decision per row, in one or
two sentences. "Where" names the ticket, the PRD section or the file that carries the reasoning. A retired row stays,
with "Retired by D-n" at the end of its text. Rows D-1 to D-4 are inherited from the operating kit.

| Id | Decision | Date | Where |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| D-1 | One orchestrator chat runs the project's work as sub-agents (the Agent tool) in git worktrees, at most three at once. No separate track sessions. | {{DATE}} | `dev-sessions/README.md`, operating kit |
| D-2 | The autonomy charter (`CHARTER.md`) binds every agent. The loop that improves agents may never touch safety rules, deny rules, authorization, the Bypass gates, the gates, the standards check's thresholds, the scoring or the charter's zero-tolerance list: a person changes those. | {{DATE}} | `CHARTER.md`, operating kit |
| D-3 | Heavy work (full suites, typechecks, production builds, browsers, timing runs) runs as cluster Jobs (`scripts/job-run.sh`, `scripts/gate-job.sh`), not in the workspace. Until those exist, one heavy job at a time in the workspace through the shared lock (`flock /tmp/heavy.lock nice -n 10 <command>`). | {{DATE}} | `dev-sessions/README.md`, operating kit |
| D-4 | Required escalations: production, uat, secrets and permissions, billing, legal, destructive data. Everything else is decided by the written default, recorded on its ticket, and closed. Production-only questions are one line on the owner's checklist, never a stream of questions. | {{DATE}} | `CHARTER.md`, operating kit |
